<article class="env-lemma" id="0C4P">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C4P">Lemma <span data-tag="0C4P">29.44.14</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to Y$ and $g : Y \to S$ be morphisms of schemes. If $S$ is quasi-compact and quasi-separated and $f$ and $g$ are projective, then $g \circ f$ is projective. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemmas <a href="/tag/07RL" data-tag="07RL">29.44.10</a> and <a href="/tag/01WC" data-tag="01WC">29.44.5</a> we see that $f$ and $g$ are quasi-projective and proper. By Lemmas <a href="/tag/01W3" data-tag="01W3">29.42.4</a> and <a href="/tag/0C4M" data-tag="0C4M">29.41.3</a> we see that $g \circ f$ is proper and quasi-projective. Thus $g \circ f$ is projective by Lemma <a href="/tag/0BCL" data-tag="0BCL">29.44.13</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>